# chat-playground is a desktop (Electron) demo: it runs the local Coding Agent
# runtime (@percena/weft-node) in the Electron main process. No remote URL, no
# backend server. Claude/Codex run locally on this machine.
#
# Real agent turns require local provider auth:
#   - Claude: `claude` CLI logged in, or @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk installed.
#   - Codex: `codex` CLI on PATH and logged in (codex app-server account/read).
#
# Nothing to configure here by default — settings (provider / cwd / permission
# mode / reasoning effort) come from the in-app panel, and the model + effort
# pickers fall back to SDK auto-detection (`listModels` → compatible gateway,
# ~/.claude/settings.json / ~/.codex/config.toml).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: demo-curated model list & effort ladder
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default the demo does NOT hardcode any model ids or effort levels — it
# shows whatever the SDK discovers. To pin a curated list instead (e.g. a fork
# that only ships a subset), set the vars below. Merge semantics:
#   - Models:  override wins → else SDK-discovered list.
#   - Efforts: override ladder wins → else built-in REASONING_EFFORT_OPTIONS.
#   - Defaults: override default model → else SDK defaultModel; the
#              default-selected effort always falls back to the SDK-detected
#              `defaultEffort` when it matches the (possibly overridden) ladder.
# All values are comma-separated; copy this file to `.env` and edit.
#
# Model picker (ids are sent verbatim to the provider gateway):
#   VITE_DEMO_MODELS_CLAUDE=claude-opus-4-6,claude-sonnet-5,glm-5.2
#   VITE_DEMO_MODELS_CODEX=gpt-5.6-terra,gpt-5.5
# Optional explicit default (must be one of the ids above):
#   VITE_DEMO_DEFAULT_MODEL_CLAUDE=claude-opus-4-6
#   VITE_DEMO_DEFAULT_MODEL_CODEX=gpt-5.6-terra
#
# Reasoning-effort ladder (slugs; labels are derived, e.g. xhigh → XHigh).
# Any slug-shaped value is passed through to the provider — the SDK does not
# gate against a fixed known set.
#   VITE_DEMO_EFFORTS_CLAUDE=low,medium,high,xhigh,max
#   VITE_DEMO_EFFORTS_CODEX=low,medium,high,xhigh
